From b635211378c570aa439c0a0864612fe4dd7458af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:22:56 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the tasks card's eye previews the task; the chevron
 keeps the details
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.22 (ask 42). The chevron and the eye opened the
same body: the command line, the details (tokens, tools, last tool,
summary) and, for a running shell, a few truncated tail lines. The
operator asked for the split the inline thread already makes: the
details behind the chevron, a preview of what the task is doing behind
the eye, with the card wide enough to read it.

The chevron opens the details, as before. The eye opens a preview: the
task's output as the agent serves it through `_claude/tasks/output`
(0056), refetched every 2 s while the task runs, its last 200 lines in a
monospace block that scrolls, with a note when earlier output was left
out. The block follows the end, as a terminal does, while the reader is
at the end or nothing was shown yet; scrolled up to read, it stays put.
The Xvfb proof found the first version opening on the first line, under
a header that already claimed it followed the end. Until the first fetch lands, or for a task whose output the agent
does not serve, the preview falls back to the feed's short tail (a
shell) or to the details (anything else), and a failed fetch says
"Preview unavailable: …" under it, so the block is never blank. While a
preview is open the card widens from 22rem to its overlay's frame, and
it goes back to its width after.

The eye keeps its tray role, per the proposal's §12 default: a watched
task still notifies when it ends. A watched row still counts as open
(TaskRow::expanded); only the chevron's own state picks the details
and the chevron's icon.

Not done here: the live TerminalView the thread draws inline for a
shell tool call. Embedding it needs the thread's entry view state in
the card; the served output covers the same text.

The output-answering test connection moved from open_log_tests.rs to
output_connection_support.rs, unchanged but for visibility, so the
preview tests share it. Two tests that said "watching shows the
details" now open the row with the chevron for the details and check
the preview on the eye (render: test_only_watched_rows_show_their_
details; progress: tasks_card_progress_keeps_the_watched_details).

Tests: tasks_card::preview_rows (the eye fetches and shows the output,
not the details, and widens the card, which narrows again after; a
running preview is refetched and stops once unwatched; a failed fetch
falls back to the tail; a long output opens on its end) and
preview::tests (the last lines). The two
that depend on the fetch were seen failing with refresh_preview made a
no-op, and the end test with scroll_to_bottom left out.
